<title>JAPAN: Japan two-year note auction lowest price at 99.92.</title>
<headline>Japan two-year note auction lowest price at 99.92.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Wednesday that its auction of 0.6 percent two-year government notes produced the following results:</p>
<p> Lowest price	 99.92   Stop rate     0.640 pct</p>
<p> Average price	99.96   Average yield 0.617 pct</p>
<p> Total bids	   255.0 billion yen</p>
<p> Accepted bids	117.0 billion yen</p>
<p> Bids accepted at lowest price 98.2758 pct</p>
<p> Issue date   Jan 20, 1997   Maturity   Jan 20, 1999</p>
</text>
